Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:32:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/34] flashnext: routed experts from an EXL3 checkpoint
 (TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_EXL3=DIR)

Loads Flash Next's routed experts from an EXL3 folder (such as turboderp's Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-exl3) and serves them
with grouped decode and prompt kernels. Off unless TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_EXL3 names a folder; the TF_EXL3_* knobs only
matter when it does.

Changes, in the order they were made:
- feat(flashnext): EXL3 routed experts' device image layout (Layout, rankLayerBytes)
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_EXL3=DIR loads routed experts from an EXL3 folder
- fix(flashnext): flashnext-exl3-experts no longer spins forever; both EXL3 GPU checks take PACK RANK
- perf(flashnext): EXL3 grouped experts route 16-pair items at every row count; TF_EXL3_GROUPED_PF=2 keeps two k tiles
  in flight
- perf(flashnext): EXL3 grouped experts load each k tile's A fragment with its words, ahead of its mma
  (TF_EXL3_GROUPED_XA, on)
- perf(flashnext): EXL3 grouped experts' lean (4 an SM) and narrow (6 an SM) programs, TF_EXL3_GROUPED_FIT, same bits
- perf(flashnext): EXL3 grouped experts through a cp.async ring (TF_EXL3_GROUPED_FIT=cp3|cp4, same bits); bench
  roofline probes
- perf(flashnext): EXL3 experts' prompt passes through x3gm v2's 64-pair items (TF_EXL3_PROMPT_ROWS, default 256)
- perf(flashnext): EXL3 grouped experts serve the 4-stage cp.async ring (TF_EXL3_GROUPED_FIT unset is cp4)

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TF_EXL3_GROUPED_FIT: cp4 (unset: the 4-stage cp.async ring, 0.69x NVFP4's time at 84 rows), base, lean, narrow or
  cp3 grouped programs (exl3_grouped.Fit), all the same bits.
- TF_EXL3_GROUPED_PF: k tiles of words a warp of the grouped kernels keeps in flight, 1 (unset) or 2.
- TF_EXL3_GROUPED_XA: 1 (unset) loads each k tile's A fragment with its words, ahead of its mma.
- TF_EXL3_PROMPT_DN: v3 (unset) or dn0.
- TF_EXL3_PROMPT_ROWS=n: TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_EXL3's routed experts on passes of n rows or more through x3gm v2's
  64-member items (exl3_fnx_prompt.cuh): each item decodes its expert's 128-column block once for up to 64 pairs and
  runs one fp32 mma chain an out...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_EXL3=DIR: the routed experts from an experts-only EXL3 folder (mul1 trellises under the EXL3
  checkpoint's names, model.safetensors.index.json beside them).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_EXL3_LAYERS=all (default) | main (the 48 decoder layers) | mtp (the MTP head's layer only).
